From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-11
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 014] panvk: v9 tessellation via gpu_prerast biblioklept

Purpose: Expose tessellationShader (with the v10 tessellation limits) and
extendedDynamicState2PatchControlPoints on v9 JM.
v10+ runs tessellation as a command stream loop (gpu_prerast_tess): each
iteration steps a chunk of patches, runs the lowered VS and the TCS, counts
and writes the tessellator output, then draws it, or runs the TES as a
lowered VS when a GS, XFB or multi-viewport follows. JM has no loop, so the
iterations are unrolled into the job chain, every job a barrier. An
iteration past the end of the draw finds nothing left: panlib_tess_step
zeroes the VS and TCS grids, new panlib_v9_compute_job_grid makes those
COMPUTE jobs NULL jobs, and the draw patch makes the empty draw a NULL job.
No CPU readback. Direct draws get exactly the iterations of the chunk plan;
indirect draws get 8 chunks. Nested TES output is cut into ranges that fit
the TES records and the GS slots. GS after tess gets its primitive ID base
from the GPU (new panlib_v9_copy32). XFB after tess is captured on layer 0.
Limits: direct draws over 4096 iterations lose the rest (logged once);
indirect draws over 8 chunks of max_patches patches lose the rest. Layered tess re-runs per layer.
shaderTessellationAndGeometryPointSize stays v10+.
Source/Reference: https://github.com/Noysz/panvk-g99-jm (commit 6ce0d46e419a, MIT; patch 0062, reference only, different single-pass design); kernels and plan from csf-v11 gpu_prerast_tess
Tested GPU: build-checked (universal Android build v6-v14); device run on Mali-G57 MC2 (gpu_id 0x90930010) pending, see worklogs/v9-jm/PROGRESS.md
Tested Kbase UAPI: JM 11.38
Mesa base range: 5a07217f + g615-v11-csf series + jm-v9 001-013
Dependencies: jm-v9 011, 012
Validation test: dEQP-VK.tessellation.*, PanProbe tessellation (pending device)

---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/libpan/draw_helper.cl b/src/panfrost/libpan/draw_helper.cl
index a217629..9bad986 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/libpan/draw_helper.cl
+++ b/src/panfrost/libpan/draw_helper.cl
@@ -1685,6 +1685,11 @@ panlib_v9_prerast_indirect(constant struct panlib_v9_prerast_patch *a)
    counts[1] = inst;
    counts[2] = first_instance;
    counts[5] = first_index;
+   if (a->chunk) {
+      global uint32_t *chunk = (global uint32_t *)a->chunk;
+      counts[8] = chunk[0];
+      counts[9] = chunk[1];
+   }
    *(global uint32_t *)a->verts_per_instance = n;
 
    v9_patch_compute_job((global uint8_t *)a->vs_job, null_job, n, inst, 1);
@@ -1724,4 +1729,19 @@ panlib_v9_prerast_indirect(constant struct panlib_v9_prerast_patch *a)
       *offset = (int32_t)(ii[0] + (first_instance / ii[2]) * ii[1]);
    }
 }
+
+/* Sizes a COMPUTE job from the {x, y, z} workgroup counts an earlier job
+ * wrote, a NULL job when one is 0: the JM form of an indirect dispatch. */
+KERNEL(1)
+panlib_v9_compute_job_grid(global uint8_t *job, constant uint32_t *grid)
+{
+   v9_patch_compute_job(job, !grid[0] || !grid[1] || !grid[2], grid[0],
+                        grid[1], grid[2]);
+}
+
+KERNEL(1)
+panlib_v9_copy32(global uint32_t *dst, constant uint32_t *src)
+{
+   *dst = *src;
+}
 #endif
